    "narrative": "As we navigate the final stretch of the 2026 season, the primary focus for Ghost Ride the WHIP remains the pursuit of stolen bases, though the daily slate is thin due to league-wide scheduling. Today\u2019s lone active starter, **Travis Bazzana**, carries an efficiency score of 52.84 against Martinez. While this sits in the marginal tier, the matchup against a 4.63 xERA arm provides enough leverage to justify the start, especially given **Travis Bazzana**\u2019s recent hot streak which adds a 100% recency weight to his baseline projection. The platoon advantage here is statistically significant, pushing his overall utility higher than his raw season averages might suggest.\n\nOur bench remains stagnant today as the rest of the core\u2014including **Corbin Carroll**, **Josh Naylor**, **James Wood**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Jose Caballero**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Cole Young**, **Griffin Conine**, and **Edwin Arroyo**\u2014are inactive due to team off-days. With **Tyler Soderstrom** remaining on the IL, our roster flexibility is currently non-existent; we are essentially forced into a \"start-one\" strategy. There were no difficult bench decisions to parse today, as the calendar effectively stripped us of the ability to chase speed via **Corbin Carroll** or **Jose Caballero**. We will monitor the health status of **Tyler Soderstrom** as we approach the final series of the season, but for today, **Travis Bazzana** is the sole engine for our Roto points.",
